// Building against a local framework checkout (fixing a preset, trying an
// unreleased change)? Uncomment the set — contrib and the handler-standard
// modules ship as one version with the framework — then `go mod tidy`. The
// kernel is its own repository and moves on its own train, so uncomment its
// line only when you are changing the kernel itself. Comment them back out
// before you ship: a replace directive never leaves your machine.
